(footprint "Speaker_SameSky_CMS-151103-088SP"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "o1next")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Same Sky CMS-151103-088SP miniature speaker -- 15 x 11 x 3 mm rectangular frame, 0.7 W (1.0 W max), 8 ohm, 90 dB, PEEK cone, Nd-Fe-B magnet, solder-pad terminals. Body and courtyard are exact, from the datasheet's SPECIFICATIONS table. **The two pads are placed, not read**: the datasheet's MECHANICAL DRAWING (page 2) is a figure, so its pad size and centre-to-centre spacing do not extract as text. They are set here to 2.0 x 2.0 mm at 5.08 mm apart -- on the 0.1 in grid so a wire jig is easy -- with the pad's outer edge 0.3 mm proud of the frame so an iron reaches it. Confirm both numbers against the drawing and this footprint is final. Pin 1 is the '+' terminal: per the datasheet the cone moves forward with positive dc on '+', so pin 1 takes SPK_P. Drawn for o1next issue #324; see the README beside it.")
	(tags "speaker audio 15x11x3mm 8ohm SameSky CMS-151103-088SP solder-pad")
